  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a 1272 Da, fully ionized corrinoid-nucleotide phosphodiester with logD -3.35, TPSA 460 Å², 11 HBD and 19 HBA; no direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for it.",
      "card_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 Caco-2 bidirectional records for the closely related corrinoid cyanocobalamin show Papp A-B = 0.1 × 10^-6 cm/s and efflux ratio 1.0 (C61; duplicate records C62/C67/C70), indicating negligible passive permeation and no efflux rescue.",
      "card_ids": ["C61", "C62", "C67", "C70"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 permeability records for other large/polar molecules (tenofovir Papp 0.15 × 10^-6 cm/s, acteoside 0.24-0.34 × 10^-6 cm/s, paeoniflorin 0.48 × 10^-6 cm/s, holotoxin below detection, So324 0.7 × 10^-6 cm/s) reinforce that extreme size and polarity yield very low intestinal permeability.",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C60", "C63", "C64", "C68", "C69"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 human B12 absorption records show only about 1-5% oral absorption for cyanocobalamin, with Caco-2 Papp 0.1 × 10^-6 cm/s; these are the most transferable corrinoid-class F evidence and are below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C48", "C50", "C54", "C55", "C57", "C58"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L1/L2 human low-F records for polar/nucleotide-like molecules (ATP 3.2-14.9%, saquinavir 4%, THU 4.1%, gemcitabine ~10%, levovirin ~10%, didanosine 17%, R1479 6-18%, phlorizin poor) are consistent with low F; rodent above-20% values are small ribonucleosides and are not transferable to this 1272 Da corrinoid phosphodiester.",
      "card_ids": ["C04", "C07", "C09", "C13", "C08", "C18", "C03", "C15", "C02", "C12", "C10", "C11", "C01", "C05", "C16", "C06", "C28", "C32", "C33"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C59", "C60", "C61", "C62", "C63", "C64", "C67", "C68", "C69", "C70"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability or query-specific permeability/efflux/metabolism measurement exists; the decision relies on transfer from corrinoid/B12 and other polar-molecule records plus physicochemical priors.",
    "B12 absorption involves intrinsic factor and receptor-mediated uptake; the query lacks cobalt and may not engage this pathway, so the exact absorption mechanism and dose dependence are uncertain.",
    "No query-specific formulation, dose, species, or human PK data are available; formulation-dependent absorption cannot be fully excluded.",
    "L5 records are Caco-2 permeability/efflux surrogates, not systemic F measurements; hepatic first-pass and renal clearance contributions remain unmeasured.",
    "C65 and C66 show moderate Caco-2 Papp for non-corrinoid glycosides, but they do not establish F >= 20% for the query and are outweighed by corrinoid-specific low-F evidence."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 Caco-2 bidirectional records for the closely related corrinoid cyanocobalamin show very low A-B permeability (0.1 × 10^-6 cm/s) with efflux ratio 1.0, and other large/polar molecules show similarly low permeability; combined with L4 human B12 absorption ~1-5% and L1/L2 low-F records, the evidence affirmatively supports F < 20% for this 1272 Da fully ionized corrinoid phosphodiester."
}

